    "explanation": "Mr Driver and Ms Rider, I have read the platform trip record, the driver's GPS trace, the in-app chat log, the fare ledger and the LTA traffic advisory, and applied the route-deviation policy.\n\nWHAT IS ESTABLISHED. The trip from Suntec City to Heartland Mall Kovan was recorded at 11.4 km against a recommended 9.9 km, a deviation of 1.50 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance (POL-RD-22; EV-TRIP-05008). The reroute was traffic-justified: the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05008-01 reports heavy traffic on the KPE towards TPE after Sims Way exit, valid 19:09-20:19 and so overlapping the trip window of 19:29-19:52, on the road and in the direction the recommended route itself uses (POL-RD-23). Mr Driver, you did give notice: your chat MSG-05008-003 was sent at 19:34:22 and read at 19:35:00, before the vehicle left the recommended route at 19:37:02 (POL-RD-21; EV-CHAT-05008, EV-TRIP-05008). But Ms Rider did not agree. POL-RD-21 makes a deviation 'agreed' only where the chat log or a call recording confirms the rider's acknowledgment, and the chat records the opposite: you asked 'I come out at Sims Ave and go Aljunied ok?' and she replied at 19:34:52 'No need, pls just stay on KPE, I don't mind the jam', repeating the objection at 19:38:22, 'Eh I said no need already, why still exit'. The exit went ahead against that refusal.\n\nWHY THIS GOES TO A HUMAN. POL-RD-24 supplies five rows and exactly one must apply. Row (a) needs the rider informed AND agreed: she was informed but did not agree. Row (b) needs the rider NOT informed: she was informed. Rows (c) and (e) need a deviation of 1 km or less: it was 1.50 km. Row (d) needs the reroute NOT traffic-justified: it was justified. No row fits, and POL-RD-24 says in terms that a case which fits no row - its own example is 'informed but the rider objected' - is escalated under POL-GEN-26. This case is that example, so I escalate it (POL-RD-24, POL-GEN-26).\n\nWHAT THAT MEANS FOR THE 1.08 SGD. ESCALATE is terminal and replaces any money outcome (POL-GEN-03): no amount is collected and none is refunded on my ruling, and the 1.08 SGD refunded to Ms Rider and recovered from Mr Driver on 21 Aug 2026 at 20:48 (EV-FARE-05008, EV-TRIP-05008) is held for the human reviewer. Mr Driver, your claim that you are owed the whole 1.08 SGD back (DRIVER_COMPENSATION) cannot succeed: the only row that would leave the driver's earnings intact is row (a), which requires the rider's agreement, and she refused; POL-RD-24 licenses no payment to the driver, and the fits-no-row rule sends the question to a human rather than restoring the charge. Your further point that escalation holds the amount rather than awarding it to the rider is correct, and I adopt it - which is why the ruling is ESCALATE, not a refund to either side. Ms Rider, your submission that the present state should simply stand as NO_ACTION is not the outcome either: because the rider was informed, no refund row of POL-RD-24 operates, and the matrix's own instruction for this combination is escalation, which is mandatory rather than a choice between NO_ACTION and a refund. Your factual points - that notice was given but not agreement (POL-RD-21), that the deviation measures 1.50 km and the excess distance fare is 1.50 x 0.72 = 1.08 SGD (POL-RD-22, POL-RD-24), and that the advisory's intersection with the recommended route was left undetermined on the package - are taken into account; I decided the intersection from the advisory's road, direction and location against the trip, as POL-RD-23 asks, and found the reroute traffic-justified. The open question the reviewer inherits is the one POL-RD-24 reserves: how a traffic-justified deviation that was notified but refused by the rider should be settled, the policy providing no row for it. No referral clause attaches to a route deviation in this version, so no referral issues."
